window.AG_PRACTICE = window.AG_PRACTICE || {};
window.AG_PRACTICE["fuhe"] = {"id":"fuhe","axis":"dx","seal":"合","scene":"art/scene-hall.jpg","title":"Combined Patterns","titleZh":"複合臟腑病證","sub":"Two organs at once — and the word that says which way it went","subZh":"二臟同病——並辨其傳變之向","mentor":{"key":"shu","nm":"Sh&#363; Ch&#299;","nmZh":"書癡","line":"\"Every one of these is two organs. The examiner is never asking which two. He is asking which one started it, and which way it travelled.\"","lineZh":"「此皆二臟同病。考官從不問是哪二臟，只問起於何臟，而傳向何方。」"},"card":{"h":"Two Organs, One Direction","hZh":"二臟一向","p":"A combined pattern is never just a list of two organs. It carries a direction — which organ failed first, and whether it overacted along the controlling cycle or insulted back against it. Overacting is Liver into Spleen or Stomach; insulting is Liver fire up into the Lung. In English examinations those two words are the trap, and swapping them is the wrong answer even when both organs are named correctly.","pZh":"複合病證非二臟之並列，必有其向：孰先失職，其傳為相乘抑或相侮。肝犯脾胃為相乘，肝火犯肺為相侮。英文考題以此二字設陷，二臟雖對而向倒置者，仍為誤。"},"items":[{"k":"mc","q":"A patient has palpitations, insomnia, poor appetite, abdominal distension, chronic light bleeding, and describes herself as worrying constantly. Which pattern, and which formula?","qZh":"心悸、失眠、納差、腹脹、慢性少量出血，自言終日憂思。何證？何方？","opts":[{"t":"Heart blood and Spleen qi deficiency — Gui Pi Tang","c":"心血虛脾氣虛 — 歸脾湯","ok":1,"note":"The formula lock the examinations use most. Three keys together: <b>worry 憂思</b> (the emotion of the Spleen), <b>palpitations with insomnia</b> (Heart blood), and <b>bleeding</b> (Spleen failing to hold blood in the vessels). Gui Pi Tang 歸脾湯 is the answer whenever those three arrive together. 考試最常之方證死鎖。三鍵並見：<b>憂思</b>（脾之志）、<b>心悸失眠</b>（心血虛）、<b>出血</b>（脾不統血）。三者俱見，即歸脾湯。"},{"t":"Heart and Kidney failing to communicate — Liu Wei Di Huang Wan","c":"心腎不交 — 六味地黃丸","ok":0,"note":"That pattern brings night heat, nocturnal emission and a sore low back, and none of them is here. Six-Flavour Rehmannia is also the formula for Liver and Kidney yin deficiency, not for this. 彼證兼夜熱、遺精、腰痠，本案皆無。且六味地黃丸為肝腎陰虛之方。"},{"t":"Spleen and Kidney yang deficiency — Si Shen Wan","c":"脾腎陽虛 — 四神丸","ok":0,"note":"That pattern is defined by daybreak diarrhoea, oedema and cold. There is no cold and no diarrhoea here. 彼證以五更瀉、水腫、虛寒為據。本案不寒不瀉。"},{"t":"Liver invading the Spleen — Xiao Yao San","c":"肝脾不和 — 逍遙散","ok":0,"note":"Liver invading Spleen is an emotional trigger with rib pain and loose stool, not palpitations with bleeding. Note the difference in emotion: <b>anger and frustration</b> for the Liver, <b>worry and overthinking</b> for the Spleen. 肝脾不和者，因情志而發，兼脅痛便溏，非悸而見血。且其志不同：肝主怒，脾主思。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Coughing blood, burning pain under the ribs, a bitter mouth, outbursts of temper, thick yellow phlegm, a wiry rapid pulse. Which pattern — and which direction word does the examination want?","qZh":"咳血、脅下灼痛、口苦、暴怒、痰黃稠、脈弦數。何證？考題所求之「向」為何字？","opts":[{"t":"Liver fire insulting the Lung — insulting 相侮, the reverse direction","c":"肝火犯肺 — 相侮，反剋之向","ok":1,"note":"Metal normally restrains Wood. When Liver fire is strong enough it turns and scorches the Lung — the reverse of the controlling cycle, called <b>insulting 相侮</b> (English: insulting, or rebellion). <i>Hemoptysis plus anger</i> is a one-symptom lock on this pattern. 金本剋木。肝火盛極，反上灼肺，逆其所勝之序，是為<b>相侮</b>。「咳血＋暴怒」一症鎖此證。"},{"t":"Liver fire insulting the Lung — overacting 相乘","c":"肝火犯肺 — 相乘","ok":0,"note":"The pattern is right and the direction word is wrong, which is exactly the trap. <b>Overacting 相乘</b> is excessive restraint <i>along</i> the controlling cycle — Liver into Spleen or Stomach. Liver into Lung runs against it. 證是而向非，此正其陷。<b>相乘</b>者，順所勝之序而過之，如肝犯脾胃。肝犯肺則逆之。"},{"t":"Lung and Kidney yin deficiency","c":"肺腎陰虛","ok":0,"note":"Also presents with blood in the cough — and the two are separated by whether the heat is full or empty. Yin deficiency brings night sweats, tidal fever, a red peeled tongue and a thready rapid pulse; this patient has a thick yellow coat, a wiry pulse and rage. 彼亦見咳血，二證之別在熱之虛實。陰虛者盜汗、潮熱、舌紅無苔、脈細數；本案苔黃厚、脈弦、且暴怒。"},{"t":"Lung heat from an exterior pathogen","c":"外邪化熱犯肺","ok":0,"note":"An exterior pattern is days old and comes with aversion to wind or cold and a floating pulse. It does not arrive on schedule after an argument. 表證病在數日，兼惡風寒、脈浮，且不因爭執而發。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"An elderly man is breathless on exertion. He says the difficulty is in drawing breath <i>in</i>, and his low back and knees ache. Tongue pale, pulse weak and deep. Diagnosis and treatment principle?","qZh":"老年男子動則氣喘，自言難在<b>吸</b>，兼腰膝痠軟。舌淡，脈沉弱。何診？何法？","opts":[{"t":"Lung and Kidney qi deficiency — tonify the Kidney to grasp qi","c":"肺腎氣虛 — 補腎納氣","ok":1,"note":"<i>Exhale more than inhale</i> is the one-symptom key. Inhalation needs the Lung to descend qi <b>and</b> the Kidney to receive and hold it; when the Kidney cannot grasp, breathing out is easy and breathing in is not. The aching low back is what lifts this out of plain Lung qi deficiency. 「呼多吸少」為一症之鍵。吸氣者，肺降之而腎納之；腎不納氣，則呼易而吸難。腰膝痠軟一證，正別於單純肺氣虛。"},{"t":"Lung qi deficiency — tonify the Lung","c":"肺氣虛 — 補肺","ok":0,"note":"Plain Lung qi deficiency has no low back or knee symptoms and the trouble is with the out-breath, not the in-breath. Those two differences are the whole question. 單純肺氣虛無腰膝之症，且其難在呼而不在吸。此二別即本題所考。"},{"t":"Lung and Spleen qi deficiency — bank up earth to generate metal","c":"肺脾氣虛 — 培土生金","ok":0,"note":"That pattern brings poor appetite, loose stool and copious phlegm — digestive signs, not lumbar ones. 彼證見納差、便溏、痰多，其候在中焦而不在腰。"},{"t":"Kidney yang deficiency — warm the yang","c":"腎陽虛 — 溫陽","ok":0,"note":"Closer, but Kidney yang deficiency alone is cold, oedema and clear copious urine. The breathing pattern is what names the Lung as the second organ. 近之，然單純腎陽虛以虛寒、水腫、小便清長為主。其喘之形，正所以並名其肺。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which single finding most reliably separates Heart and Kidney failing to communicate from Heart and Kidney yang deficiency?","qZh":"心腎不交與心腎陽虛，何證最足以別之？","opts":[{"t":"Whether the palpitations are fast or slow, and whether there is oedema","c":"心悸之遲速，及有無水腫","ok":1,"note":"The board separates this pair on three axes: <b>palpitations</b> fast (disconnect) versus slow (yang deficiency); <b>oedema</b> absent versus present and pitting; <b>temperature</b> five-centre heat versus cold limbs. Reproductive signs follow the same split — nocturnal emission versus impotence. One is a yin pattern, the other a yang pattern. 考試以三軸別之：<b>心悸</b>快（不交）／慢（陽虛）；<b>水腫</b>無／有而凹陷；<b>寒熱</b>五心煩熱／四肢冰冷。生殖之候亦然：遺精／陽痿。一屬陰虛，一屬陽虛。"},{"t":"Whether the patient has insomnia","c":"有無失眠","ok":0,"note":"Both can disturb sleep. A finding shared by two patterns cannot separate them — look for the one that differs. 二證俱能擾眠。二證所共者不能為別，當求其異。"},{"t":"Whether the low back aches","c":"腰痠與否","ok":0,"note":"Both involve the Kidney, so both can ache. Again, a shared finding. 二證俱病在腎，皆可腰痠。此亦其所共者。"},{"t":"Whether the tongue has a coating","c":"舌有苔無苔","ok":0,"note":"Useful, but less decisive than the three-axis comparison and easily confounded. The examination asks for palpitation rate, oedema and temperature. 雖有其用，然不若三軸之明，且易受他因所擾。考題所求者，悸之遲速、腫、寒熱三事。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each combined pattern to the formula the examinations lock it to.","qZh":"方證死鎖：各證配其方。","pairs":[{"l":"Heart blood + Spleen qi deficiency","lZh":"心血虛脾氣虛","r":"Gui Pi Tang","rZh":"歸脾湯"},{"l":"Liver invading the Spleen (IBS)","lZh":"肝脾不和（腸易激）","r":"Xiao Yao San","rZh":"逍遙散"},{"l":"Liver invading the Stomach (GERD)","lZh":"肝胃不和（胃食道逆流）","r":"Chai Hu Shu Gan San","rZh":"柴胡疏肝散"},{"l":"Lung and Kidney yin deficiency","lZh":"肺腎陰虛","r":"Bai He Gu Jin Tang","rZh":"百合固金湯"},{"l":"Liver and Kidney yin deficiency","lZh":"肝腎陰虛","r":"Liu Wei Di Huang Wan","rZh":"六味地黃丸"},{"l":"Lung and Spleen qi deficiency","lZh":"肺脾氣虛","r":"Liu Jun Zi Tang","rZh":"六君子湯"}],"note":"These are single-answer questions on the board, so the pairs are worth holding as pairs. Two more to add: Spleen and Kidney yang deficiency takes Si Shen Wan with Li Zhong Wan 四神丸＋理中丸, and Liver blood with Kidney essence depletion takes Gui Lu Er Xian Jiao 龜鹿二仙膠. 此為單選必考，宜成對而記。尚有二事：脾腎陽虛用四神丸合理中丸，肝血腎精虧虛用龜鹿二仙膠。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Which of these deficiency patterns does <i>not</i> exist in TCM theory?","qZh":"下列虛證，何者於中醫理論中並不存在？","opts":[{"t":"Spleen blood deficiency","c":"脾血虛","ok":1,"note":"There is no Spleen blood deficiency pattern — the Spleen <i>makes</i> blood and <i>holds</i> it, but the deficiency patterns named for it are qi, yang and yin. The board tests this by putting an impossible pattern among the options. The empty cells worth memorising: the Liver has no qi or yang deficiency; the Spleen and Kidney have no blood deficiency; the Lung has no yang or blood deficiency; the Stomach has no yang deficiency. 中醫無「脾血虛」之證：脾能生血、統血，而其虛證則為氣、陽、陰。考題以不存在之證混於選項以試之。空格宜記：肝無氣虛陽虛，脾腎無血虛，肺無陽虛血虛，胃無陽虛。"},{"t":"Liver blood deficiency","c":"肝血虛","ok":0,"note":"Standard and common — dry eyes, blurred vision, numbness, cramp, brittle nails, scanty menses. 常見之證：目乾、視糊、麻木、拘攣、爪脆、經少。"},{"t":"Kidney yin deficiency","c":"腎陰虛","ok":0,"note":"Standard — tinnitus, night sweats, sore low back, five-centre heat. 常證：耳鳴、盜汗、腰痠、五心煩熱。"},{"t":"Stomach yin deficiency","c":"胃陰虛","ok":0,"note":"Standard — hungry but no desire to eat, dry mouth, a peeled tongue centre. 常證：飢不欲食、口乾、舌中剝苔。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"A woman has diarrhoea before dawn every day, pitting oedema of the legs, a cold aching low back, and passes clear urine several times a night. Tongue pale and swollen, pulse deep and slow. Which pattern?","qZh":"婦人每日黎明前泄瀉，下肢凹陷性水腫，腰膝冷痛，夜溺清長數次。舌淡胖，脈沉遲。何證？","opts":[{"t":"Spleen and Kidney yang deficiency","c":"脾腎陽虛","ok":1,"note":"<i>Daybreak diarrhoea</i> — cock-crow diarrhoea in the English wording — is the signature. The fifth watch is when yin is spent and yang should rise; a patient whose gate-of-life fire is low loses the bowel at exactly that hour. Formula: Si Shen Wan with Li Zhong Wan 四神丸＋理中丸. 「五更泄瀉」（英作 daybreak / cock-crow diarrhea）為其標誌。五更者陰盡陽生之時；命門火衰則於此時失其固。方用四神丸合理中丸。"},{"t":"Spleen qi deficiency","c":"脾氣虛","ok":0,"note":"Spleen qi deficiency gives loose stool at no particular hour, with no oedema, no cold low back and no nocturnal urination. The hour and the back are what add the Kidney. 脾氣虛之便溏不擇時，且無水腫、無腰冷、無夜尿。時辰與腰膝二證，正所以並及於腎。"},{"t":"Damp-heat in the Intestines","c":"腸道濕熱","ok":0,"note":"That diarrhoea is urgent, foul, burning on the way out, with a bitter mouth, dark scanty urine, a greasy yellow coat and a rapid pulse. Every one is the opposite here. 彼瀉急迫穢臭、肛門灼熱，兼口苦、尿短赤、苔黃膩、脈數。本案一一相反。"},{"t":"Liver invading the Spleen","c":"肝脾不和","ok":0,"note":"That one is triggered by emotion, brings rib distension, and alternates between constipation and loose stool. It does not keep an appointment at the fifth watch. 彼因情志而發，兼脅脹，且便秘泄瀉交替。其發不守五更之時。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Blurred vision together with tinnitus points at which pair of organs, and why?","qZh":"視物模糊兼耳鳴，指向何二臟？其理安在？","opts":[{"t":"Liver and Kidney — the Liver opens into the eyes and the Kidney governs the ears","c":"肝與腎 — 肝開竅於目，腎主耳","ok":1,"note":"Two organs, two orifices, one sentence. This pairing is a standard board key for Liver and Kidney yin deficiency, treated with Liu Wei Di Huang Wan 六味地黃丸. The wider principle is <i>Liver and Kidney share a source</i> 乙癸同源: Kidney essence produces Liver blood, so the two run short together. 二臟、二竅，一語可決。此為肝腎陰虛之考點，方用六味地黃丸。其理在乙癸同源：腎精化肝血，故二者同虛。"},{"t":"Heart and Liver","c":"心與肝","ok":0,"note":"Heart and Liver blood deficiency does blur vision — but it brings palpitations, forgetting and numbness rather than tinnitus, and it has no heat signs at all. 心肝血虛誠能視糊，然兼心悸、健忘、麻木，而不見耳鳴，且通身無熱。"},{"t":"Lung and Kidney","c":"肺與腎","ok":0,"note":"That pair shows in breathing and in the voice, not in the eyes. 此對之候在息在聲，不在目。"},{"t":"Spleen and Kidney","c":"脾與腎","ok":0,"note":"That pair shows in the stool, the oedema and the cold. 此對之候在便、在腫、在寒。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Overacting and insulting are opposite directions on the controlling cycle. Which pairing is stated correctly?","qZh":"相乘與相侮，其向相反。下列何者為是？","opts":[{"t":"Liver overacting on the Spleen; Liver fire insulting the Lung","c":"肝乘脾；肝火侮肺","ok":1,"note":"Wood normally restrains Earth, so Liver into Spleen is excessive restraint <b>along</b> the cycle — overacting 相乘. Metal normally restrains Wood, so Liver fire into Lung runs <b>against</b> it — insulting 相侮. In examination options the two words are swapped to make the wrong answer; the organs alone will not save you. 木本剋土，肝犯脾者，順其序而過之，是為相乘。金本剋木，肝火犯肺者，逆其序而反之，是為相侮。考題以二字互易為誤答，但識二臟者不足以自保。"},{"t":"Liver insulting the Spleen; Liver fire overacting on the Lung","c":"肝侮脾；肝火乘肺","ok":0,"note":"Both directions reversed — and this is the option written specifically to be chosen by someone who knows the organs and not the cycle. 二向俱倒。此選項正為識臟而不識五行之序者而設。"},{"t":"The Spleen overacting on the Liver; the Lung insulting the Liver","c":"脾乘肝；肺侮肝","ok":0,"note":"Earth does not restrain Wood and Metal restraining Wood is the normal direction, not insulting. Both halves are wrong. 土不剋木；金剋木為常序，非侮。二者皆非。"},{"t":"Both terms mean the same thing","c":"二者同義","ok":0,"note":"They are opposites, and the distinction is examined directly. 二者相反，且為直接考點。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"A patient has chronic cough with copious phlegm, poor appetite, abdominal distension and loose stool. Which five-phase relationship names the treatment principle?","qZh":"久咳痰多，兼納差、腹脹、便溏。此屬五行何種關係？其治法何名？","opts":[{"t":"Mother and child — bank up earth to generate metal 培土生金","c":"母子關係 — 培土生金","ok":1,"note":"Earth is the mother of Metal, so the Spleen is the mother of the Lung. Build the mother and the child is fed: strengthen the Spleen and the Lung recovers, which is why the formula is Liu Jun Zi Tang 六君子湯 rather than a Lung formula. The principle has a name worth keeping — <b>培土生金</b>. 土生金，故脾為肺之母。補其母則子受其養：健脾而肺自復，故方取六君子湯而不取肺劑。其法有名，曰<b>培土生金</b>。"},{"t":"Controlling cycle — the Spleen overacting on the Lung","c":"相剋 — 脾乘肺","ok":0,"note":"Earth generates Metal, it does not restrain it. There is no controlling relationship between them at all. 土生金，非剋金。二者本無相剋之屬。"},{"t":"Insulting — the Lung insulting the Spleen","c":"相侮 — 肺侮脾","ok":0,"note":"Insulting is a reversal of the controlling cycle, and there is no controlling cycle between these two to reverse. 相侮者，反其所勝之序；二者本無相剋，何反之有。"},{"t":"No relationship — the two illnesses are unconnected","c":"無所關涉 — 二病各不相干","ok":0,"note":"Then you would write two prescriptions. The point of the mother-child relationship is that one treatment reaches both. 若然，則出二方。母子之義，正在一治而及其二。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Three yang collapses are examined as a set. Which mapping is correct?","qZh":"三陽崩脫為必考之組。下列配對何者為是？","opts":[{"t":"Heart yang collapse ≈ heart attack; Spleen qi failing to hold blood ≈ haemorrhage; Kidney yang collapse ≈ respiratory failure","c":"心陽暴脫≈心臟病發；脾氣不統血≈大出血；腎陽崩≈呼吸衰竭","ok":1,"note":"All three are emergencies. The revival points examined with them are <b>DU26 人中, DU25 素髎 and KI1 湧泉</b> — restore yang and secure what is collapsing. In any real clinic these are ambulance situations first and point selections second. 三者皆急症。所配回陽固脫之穴為<b>人中 DU26、素髎 DU25、湧泉 KI1</b>。臨證所先者，急救轉送；穴之選在其後。"},{"t":"Heart yang collapse ≈ respiratory failure; Kidney yang collapse ≈ heart attack","c":"心陽暴脫≈呼吸衰竭；腎陽崩≈心臟病發","ok":0,"note":"Swapped. The Kidney grasps qi, so its collapse shows in breathing; the Heart governs the vessels, so its collapse shows in circulation. 二者互易。腎主納氣，其脫見於息；心主血脈，其脫見於血行。"},{"t":"Lung yang collapse ≈ haemorrhage","c":"肺陽暴脫≈大出血","ok":0,"note":"There is no Lung yang deficiency pattern at all, so there is no Lung yang collapse. This is the empty-cell rule reappearing. 肺本無陽虛之證，故無肺陽暴脫。此即空格之例復現。"},{"t":"All three are treated with the same single point","c":"三者同取一穴","ok":0,"note":"They share a revival strategy and a group of points, not one point — and they are distinguished from one another by mechanism. 其法與穴群雖同，非止一穴；且三者之機各異，必當分辨。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each one-symptom key to the pattern it locks.","qZh":"一症鎖病：各鍵配其證。","pairs":[{"l":"Coughing blood with rage","lZh":"咳血兼暴怒","r":"Liver fire insulting the Lung","rZh":"肝火犯肺"},{"l":"Diarrhoea before dawn","lZh":"五更泄瀉","r":"Spleen and Kidney yang deficiency","rZh":"脾腎陽虛"},{"l":"Breathing out easier than in","lZh":"呼多吸少","r":"Lung and Kidney qi deficiency","rZh":"肺腎氣虛"},{"l":"Blurred vision with tinnitus","lZh":"視糊兼耳鳴","r":"Liver and Kidney yin deficiency","rZh":"肝腎陰虛"},{"l":"Insomnia, emission, night heat","lZh":"失眠、遺精、夜熱","r":"Heart and Kidney not communicating","rZh":"心腎不交"}],"note":"These five are the fastest marks on the paper. Each is a single distinctive finding that no neighbouring pattern shares, so when one appears the answer is settled before you have read the rest of the stem. 此五者，卷上得分最速者也。各為一證所獨有，鄰證不與；見其一，未讀其餘而答已定。"}]};
